				1582,
				2
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Extract inline JSON blocks to avoid macro recursion limit\n\nThe `ConstructSandboxConfiguration` function builds the entire `ISandboxConfiguration` payload in a single deeply-nested `json!()` macro invocation. As the `profiles` and `productConfiguration` sections grew, the macro expansion exceeded Rust's recursion limit, causing compilation failures on certain toolchain versions.\n\nExtract the `nls`, `productConfiguration`, `os`, and `profiles` sub-objects into separate `json!()` calls bound to local variables (`NlsSection`, `ProductConfig`, `OsSection`, `ProfilesSection`), then reference them by name in the outer `json!()` invocation. This breaks the single deep expansion into multiple shallow ones, staying well within the recursion limit without changing any emitted values.\n\nNo behavioral change — all pre-built variables produce identical JSON to the previously inlined blocks.",
			"SHA": "78820a9ee66e89a88169dab5bf7acb7b986c1eb3"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-22T05:35:25Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1582,
				19
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Complete Cocoon extension host bridge across providers, boot, and keyboard\n\nImplement the gRPC and provider-infrastructure layer for four extension-host features that Mountain forwards to Cocoon, three complementary improvements, and one build-config update.\n\n**Extension provider features:**\n\n- **Inline completion items** (GitHub Copilot, Roo Code, Continue): New `InlineCompletionItem` / `InlineCompletionContext` messages in Vine.proto, gRPC handler in `ProvideInlineCompletionItems.rs`, and `$provideInlineCompletionItems` dispatch from `FeatureMethods.rs` to Cocoon's registered provider. Registration flows through the generic notification dispatcher via `register_inline_completion_item_provider`.\n\n- **File decorations from extensions**: `DecorationsGet` in `Decoration.rs` falls back to `ProvideFileDecoration` via Cocoon gRPC when the in-memory store has no entry, populating git-status badges, error markers, and other extension-contributed decorations on demand.\n\n- **Terminal lifecycle sync**: `TerminalProvider.rs` emits `$acceptTerminalOpened` / `$acceptTerminalClosed` notifications to Cocoon so `vscode.window.terminals` stays current for terminals created from the UI (not just via the extension API).\n\n- **Webview message forwarding**: `Messaging.rs` implements the forward path for `acquireVsCodeApi().postMessage()` calls from extension iframes, sending them as `webview.message` notifications to Cocoon so the extension host's `onDidReceiveMessage` subscriber fires. `remove_webview_message_listener_impl` is now a logging stub rather than a no-op.\n\n**Boot performance and crash fixes:**\n\n- **Extension manifest cache (B7.P08)**: New `LoadFromCache.rs` reads a pre-baked `extensions.manifest.json` blob in a single `fs::read`, reducing extension-scan boot time from ~1200 ms to <50 ms. Falls back gracefully to the live `ScanAndPopulateExtensions` path on cache miss, staleness (>10 min), or corruption. The cache file is produced by `Maintain/Build/Manifest/PreBake.ts` during `beforeBundleCommand`.\n\n- **WKWebView NSUndoManager suppression**: `TauriBuild.rs` disables the macOS default menu (which pre-installs Edit > Undo/Redo). `WindowBuild.rs` injects a capture-phase keydown listener that `preventDefault()`s Cmd+Z/Cmd+Y before the webview's internal responder chain dispatches undo:/redo:, preventing WKWebView's NSUndoManager from competing with Monaco's undo stack.\n\n- **Profiles configuration**: `InitializationData.rs` adds the `INativeWindowConfiguration.profiles` section with all required URI fields (`languageModelsResource`, `agentPluginsHome`, `cacheHome`, etc.) to prevent the `TypeError: undefined is not an object (evaluating 'M.revive(o.languageModelsResource).with')` crash during workbench initialisation. Also adds `sqmId`, `devDeviceId`, and `isPortable` as defensive non-optional fields.\n\n**Build:** `tauri.conf.json` adds `node Maintain/Build/Manifest/PreBake.ts` to the `beforeBundleCommand` pipeline.\n\nCloses the Mountain side of the inline-completion provider circuit and addresses the workbench profile crash (VS Code desktop-mode init).",
			"SHA": "8db51dd0dc8da12799836d25faaf61658c445a52"
		},
